# state: any   (golden 9153c63300da, the same as gta-3.route)
# Grand Theft Auto III (5454000E): a DRIVING route (lane.gta3drive1017, #433).
# NOT PROVEN until a run's frames show the car moving: frames minutes apart at
# different places, radar turning. gta-3.route is the on-foot measurement and
# stays as it is.
#
# Boot: copied verbatim from gta-3.route through its `waitfor fist-hud` (see
# that file's header for why there is no START and why the mark is gated on
# the weapon icon). The crop is the same file, refs/gta-3-drive/fist-hud.png =
# refs/gta-3/fist-hud.png.
#
# Entry: the spawn frame of 1-1791792686-lane.local-32437
# (route-frames/012712-gameplay.png) shows the Kuruma about 3 m to Claude's
# right, with the mission's blue marker over it. GTA III's enter/exit is Y on
# the Xbox pad. The game takes the nearest upright car within 10 units of the
# player (re3 CPlayerInfo::FindClosestCarSectorList, `dist <= 10.0f`), so one
# Y press walks Claude to its door and in. The 7 s after it lets 8-Ball take
# the passenger seat (the first mission's objective) before the throttle.
# `mark gameplay` is after the entry, so the scored window is driving.
#
# Driving: RT accelerates (pad.sh: the triggers are not swapped; max is full
# throttle), LT brakes and reverses, LX steers. Equal left and right pulses
# hold the heading on average. Every third lap backs up with the wheel turned
# (RT released, LT held) so a wall or a lamp post cannot hold the car. Never
# Y after the entry (it would exit), never START or BACK.
#
wait 55
repeat 4 {
    press A 300
    wait 5
}
shot introskip
repeat 12 {
    press A 300
    wait 5
}
shot pregameplay
waitfor fist-hud 60 1020,88,140,130 20
shot onfoot
press Y 300
wait 7
shot incar
mark gameplay
repeat forever {
    repeat 3 {
        axis RT max
        wait 4
        axis LX min
        wait 0.6
        axis LX mid
        wait 3
        axis LX max
        wait 0.6
        axis LX mid
        wait 2
    }
    shot drive
    axis RT min
    axis LT max
    axis LX max
    wait 2
    axis LT min
    axis LX mid
}
